1erf|n|A falling out, happening, or coming to pass; hence, that which falls out or happens; occurrence; incident. ; A favorable opportunity; a convenient or timely chance; convenience. ; An occurrence or condition of affairs which brings with it some unlooked-for event; that which incidentally brings to pass an event, without being its efficient cause or sufficient reason; accidental or incidental cause. ; Need; exigency; requirement; necessity; as, I have no occasion for firearms. ; A reason or excuse; a motive; a persuasion.	a:1plf,81,4~1plf,81,4
